    "statement": "With Q_18(t)=(P(t)-18)_+, split X_18=sum_(t!=1)Q_18(t)R(t)=A_18+Y_18, where A_18=sum_(t!=1,R(t)>0)Q_18(t)<=(n-1)^2 and Y_18=sum_(t!=1)Q_18(t)(R(t)-1)_+. Therefore the exact residual estimate 17Y_18<=283n^2+34n-17, or the stronger Y_18<=16n^2, implies the C36' target. Every positive Y_18 record is both a rich product event and an additional quotient-collision event.",
